00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:12.210
to invest in this area.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:22.510
Now, this is the role of machine
learning in our research.

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:25.820
So the problem that we attacked
with machine learning--

00:16:25.820 --> 00:16:28.690
first of all, we are doing
ML on small or medium data

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:30.160
sets for a moment.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.850
We are expanding now
to larger data sets.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:34.810
And I'm mentioning this
because you will not

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:38.260
see here a deep learning
model, because, by definition,

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.860
to do deep learning, you need
to have a massive data set.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:46.650
So here we are working with
small and medium data sets.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.220
Based on the for
transaction cost,

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:50.720
redemption at risk,
tradable volume,

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.640
was our big successful
story of last year.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:57.070
So to one component
transaction cost

00:16:57.070 --> 00:17:00.120
must be able to forecast
the T-plus-1 tradable volume

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:02.170
of a specific [INAUDIBLE].

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.859
And we found a lot of
benefits in the model

00:17:05.859 --> 00:17:07.150
leveraging machine learning.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:12.640
And security similarity--
the concept of went into use.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.390
Machine learning tools we used--
primary regularized linear

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:18.940
regression, random forest,
and gradient-boosting trees.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:22.355
Despite that, we, in
the lab, now in the lab,

00:17:22.355 --> 00:17:23.980
we have a neural
network implementation

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.690
on some of these models.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.109
Number four, the use of suspect.

00:17:28.109 --> 00:17:30.690
So the neural network
implementation,

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:33.190
despite that they are improving
the performance with respect

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.790
to random forest, but not
crazy, because data set is still

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.540
medium-sized, we have the
problem of interpretability.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:45.550
So we prefer, for a moment,
to roll out a random forest

00:17:45.550 --> 00:17:46.690
approach.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.700
And with respect to the
neural network where

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.117
we are keeping
this in the lab, we

00:17:50.117 --> 00:17:51.810
